title: Raising the Colours
text: Three colours, one filter, one flag.
trick: three white copies (two splitters, a reflector and a 135-degree bender from the bottom) cross at one multi-filter; the one coming down leaves red, the one from the side blue, the diagonal one green; a reflector and a bender then lay red and green along the flag beside blue, so no target line points back at the junction
motif: pictogram (a flag on a pole: the flag is occupied squares, the pole a wall; the laser line is the halyard to the pole top)
expect: shared>=2
proof: not proved; no other solution found in 300 s
